From: Ghaf contributors <ghaf@tii.ae>
Subject: [PATCH] compositor: poll implicit DMA-BUF fences on Tegra

The Tegra DMA-BUF implicit-fence poll implementation can make the buffer
readable without waking an epoll waiter. COSMIC then leaves the surface commit
blocked until unrelated input wakes calloop; animated clients consequently
advance only while the pointer moves.

When COSMIC_POLL_DMABUF_FENCES is set, replace the implicit-fence fd event
source with a short-lived timer that polls the same DMA-BUF planes every 2 ms.
Keep the Smithay transaction blocked until every plane really reports readable,
so this does not weaken implicit synchronization or sample unfinished buffers.
Explicit syncobj acquire points retain their existing event-driven path.
